{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of the surgery team members. You’re here today for your scheduled pancreas and kidney transplant, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been waiting for this call for months. Is everything set for surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry, but I have some news. The donor organs were evaluated and unfortunately weren’t suitable for transplant. They didn’t meet the safety or function criteria."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… I was really hoping this would happen. Does that mean I’m not getting the transplant at all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not today. You’re still fully listed and active for transplant. This just means we have to wait for another donor match. It’s disappointing, but not uncommon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I guess I just feel let down. I’ve been doing everything right—my PD, my meds, my diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You absolutely have. Your labs look stable—creatinine is high as expected, but no signs of infection or acute issues. Your chest X-ray also looks clear, which is good for surgical clearance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that DNR status on file since last time. Does that affect anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s actually something we discussed with the team. Since you were admitted for transplant, we temporarily reversed your DNR status for the perioperative period, just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see. But since there’s no surgery, does that mean my DNR is back in place?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, since no procedure is happening, your current wishes stand. The transplant clinic will follow up with you about the MOLST form and your code status."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I just want to be clear about what happens next."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. You’ll go home today. You should continue your peritoneal dialysis as usual and take all your regular medications, including insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on domperidone before—can I restart that? It helps with my gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve added domperidone to your discharge list—10 mg three times a day before meals. It’s safe with your current meds and should help with fullness and nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. And if I get sick or something changes, I should call the transplant clinic, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Any hospitalization, illness, or even insurance changes—let them know. It could affect your listing status."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. So no surgery today, but I’m still on the list and just waiting for the next call."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. We know it’s frustrating, but your spot hasn’t changed. We’ll keep supporting you until the right match comes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for explaining everything. I was nervous coming in, but I feel better knowing what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2182-06-08 20:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You should be able to go home in the next hour or so."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2182-06-08 21:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—should I monitor my blood sugar more closely now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2182-06-08 21:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep checking as usual. Your HbA1c is 6.4%, which is good control. Just stick with your glargine and sliding scale as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2182-06-08 21:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my PD—no changes there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2182-06-08 21:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No changes. Continue your peritoneal dialysis exactly as you do at home. If you notice any signs of infection around the catheter, call your nephrologist right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2182-06-08 21:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for walking me through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2182-06-08 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll be in touch if anything changes. Take care, and we’ll see you when the next opportunity comes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2182-06-08 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be ready. Thank you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2182-06-08 20:16:00",
    "admission_end": "2182-06-09 09:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for a planned pancreas and kidney transplant but the procedure was canceled due to the donor organs being deemed unsuitable. She had been previously designated DNR/DNI, and her code status was temporarily reversed for the perioperative period, though no surgery occurred. Her condition remained stable throughout the brief admission, with no acute findings on physical exam or chest imaging. She was discharged home with instructions to resume peritoneal dialysis and all home medications, including a reinstated domperidone regimen for gastroparesis. The transplant clinic was notified of her ongoing DNR status via the MOLST form, and she was advised to report any medical changes that could affect her transplant eligibility.",
